{"id":10974,"date":"2024-02-11T08:23:18","date_gmt":"2024-02-11T16:23:18","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=10974"},"modified":"2024-08-13T20:08:43","modified_gmt":"2024-08-14T03:08:43","slug":"0-6-calibrating-the-color-sensor-jrotc","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-6-calibrating-the-color-sensor-jrotc\/","title":{"rendered":"0.6: Calibrating the Color Sensor (JROTC ed.)"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22132128f09\" name=\"6a22132128f09\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is the Color Sensor?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) is equipped with two color sensors on the bottom of the drone. When your drone is powered on, you may have noticed the two bright lights projected underneath the drone. Those lights help your color sensors detect how much red, green, and blue light are being reflected. You will learn more about how the color sensor works in a later lesson.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10979&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Important:<\/strong> The color sensors will only work when the drone has landed on a surface. The color sensors cannot detect the surface underneath during flight.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10978&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22132129020\" name=\"6a22132129020\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Materials<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To calibrate the color sensor, you will need:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>the drone<\/li>\n<li>a battery<\/li>\n<li>8 color cards (included in the box)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>You will <strong>not<\/strong> need the Smart Controller to calibrate the color sensor.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22132129083\" name=\"6a22132129083\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Arrange the color cards in the following order:\u00a0 WHITE, BLACK, RED, YELLOW, GREEN, LIGHT BLUE, BLUE, PURPLE.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10997&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221321290fb\" name=\"6a221321290fb\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Calibrate<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<strong>Step 1: Initiate the Color Calibration Sequence<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Connect the battery to the drone and place it on the table. Press the action button on the drone five (5) times. Wait for the sound sequence. \ud83c\udfb6[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10989&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Step 2: Use the Action Item to Calibrate the First Color<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The color calibration sequence will calibrate each color one at a time in the order listed above. Place the drone on the white card and press the action button once.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10995&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Step 3: Repeat for Each Color<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The LED on the drone will change to the next color that needs to be calibrated. Place the drone on the color before pressing the action button.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Note:<\/strong> If the LED turns off, this is for the black color card![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10996&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=-byw7c8YT68&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Calibrating the Color Sensors on CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.)&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22132129153\" name=\"6a22132129153\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Verifying Your Calibration<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]When you finish the color calibration, you will hear another sound sequence \ud83c\udfb6. Now your color sensor is ready to use!<\/p>\n<p>You can verify that your sensor is working correctly by turning on your controller and switching the color status screen. Place your drone on each of the color cards and check your controller to see if it is reading correctly.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Note:<\/strong> there will be some variation that happens with this calibration. Be sure to calibrate again when you get into Blockly or Python. You will get more accurate readings from there.<\/p>\n<p>You will learn where to see the values and program with the color sensor in later lessons. Move ahead to the next lesson to learn about your controller and how to access the color data.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11169&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 6 What is the Color Sensor? [vc_column_text]CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) is equipped with two color sensors on the bottom of the drone. When your drone is powered on,&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-6-calibrating-the-color-sensor-jrotc\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":11245,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":10878,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[10991,14401,10989],"class_list":["post-10974","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-calibrate","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-color-sensor","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10974","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":32,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10974\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12519,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10974\/revisions\/12519"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/11245"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=10974"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=10974"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=10974"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}